From a39e59b0924bc50e5d61126c45ba48a9818c1e2b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yekai pan <pyk@seas.upenn.edu>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 04:38:39 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 25/25] l2r-local: rcgmp pin: mlir-rcgmp cc73b218 (upstream #49
 and #50)

Move the mlir-rcgmp commit that the build fetches from ca288d5e to
cc73b218, upstream mlir-rcgmp's main with #49 (vectorized heap paths of
AND, OR and XOR) and #50 (division without a remainder when only the
quotient is wanted). Only runtime/Bitwise.cppm and runtime/Divide.cppm
change between the two commits (and their tests); no dialect, conversion
or C API file changes, so every rcgmp operation lowers as before.

Effect: a bignum benchmark dominated by quotients (lean2rr's L11) runs
33.50G instructions instead of 40.10G (-16%): mpn_tdiv_qr's
divide-and-conquer remainder is no longer computed when only the
quotient is used.

A local stand-in until upstream Reussir moves its pin (as it did for
#48 in #804); dropped then.
---
 cmake/RCGMP.cmake | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/cmake/RCGMP.cmake b/cmake/RCGMP.cmake
index ae4124e3..7bc28bdc 100644
--- a/cmake/RCGMP.cmake
+++ b/cmake/RCGMP.cmake
@@ -38,7 +38,7 @@ endforeach()
 FetchContent_Declare(
   rcgmp
   GIT_REPOSITORY https://github.com/reussir-lang/mlir-rcgmp.git
-  GIT_TAG ca288d5ee91304265b79dfac10b2c24aa1f86e99
+  GIT_TAG cc73b218f6ce90b005744c4e94b2b32a0e30c725
   # Only the libraries Reussir links are built; `rcgmp-opt` is not.
   EXCLUDE_FROM_ALL
 )
